{"id": "EUVD-2026-71994", "enisaUuid": "747be530-0e3e-32c0-85b5-22082d17748a", "description": "Bilibili Desktop through 1.18.0 disables TLS certificate verification process-wide and executes unsigned remote JavaScript configuration without integrity checks. An attacker in an on-path network position can intercept configuration fetches, inject arbitrary JavaScript executed in the renderer with access to the privileged IPC bridge, and execute system commands or steal login credentials.", "datePublished": "2026-09-05T11:38:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-08T18:15:27", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/LeoWSY-hashblue/bilibili-desktop-tls-disabled-rce", "https://github.com/LeoWSY-hashblue/bilibili-desktop-tls-disabled-rce/blob/main/advisory.md", "https://app.bilibili.com/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/bilibili-desktop-through-1.18.0-remote-code-execution-via-tls-verification-bypass"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-86185", "GHSA-fqf8-xgqj-hc63"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f16dd5f-e454-36fd-8981-ccce46a16753", "product": {"name": "Bilibili Desktop", "vendor": {"name": "Bilibili"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.18.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2bb75893-d5ef-3949-b8b5-1b644b742e30", "vendor": {"name": "Bilibili"}}], "isExploited": false}